   131→	/**
   132→	 * Generates a random circle packing of the input shape by generating random
   133→	 * points one-by-one and calculating the maximum radius a circle at each point
   134→	 * can have (such that it's tangent to its nearest circle or a shape vertex).
   135→	 * <p>
   136→	 * Notably, the {@code points} argument defines the number of random point
   137→	 * attempts (or circle attempts), and not the number of circles in the final
   138→	 * packing output, since a point is rejected if it lies in an existing circle or
   139→	 * whose nearest circle is less than minRadius distance away. In other words,
   140→	 * {@code points} defines the maximum number of circles the packing can have; in
   141→	 * practice, the packing will contain somewhat fewer circles.
   142→	 * <p>
   143→	 * Circles in this packing do not overlap and are contained entirely within the
   144→	 * shape. However, not every circle is necessarily tangent to other circles (in
   145→	 * which case, such a circle will be tangent to a shape vertex).
   146→	 * 
   147→	 * @param shape             the shape from which to generate a circle packing
   148→	 * @param points            number of random points to generate (this is not the
   149→	 *                          number of circles in the packing).
   150→	 * @param minRadius         filter (however not simply applied at the end, so
   151→	 *                          affects how the packing operates during packing)
   152→	 * @param triangulatePoints when true, triangulates an initial random point set
   153→	 *                          and uses triangle centroids as the random point set
   154→	 *                          instead; this results in a packing that covers the
   155→	 *                          shape more evenly (particularly when points is
   156→	 *                          small), which is sometimes desirable
   157→	 * @return A list of PVectors, each representing one circle: (.x, .y) represent
   158→	 *         the center point and .z represents radius.
   159→	 */
   160→	public static List<PVector> stochasticPack(final PShape shape, final int points, final double minRadius, boolean triangulatePoints) {
   161→		return stochasticPack(shape, points, minRadius, triangulatePoints, System.nanoTime());
   162→	}
