    33→/**
    34→ * A 'faster' CoverTree implementation based on the paper:
    35→ * 
    36→ * "Faster Cover Trees", Mike Izbicki, Christian R. Shelton,
    37→ * Proceedings of the 32nd International Conference on Machine Learning,
    38→ * Lille, France, 2015. 
    39→ * 
    40→ * Changes over original algorithms:
    41→ *  - findNearestNeighbour compares
    42→ *  	if (d(y, x) greater (d(_x_, q.point()) - q.maxdist(this)))
    43→ *    instead of 
    44→ *      if (d(y, x) greater (d(_y_, q.point()) - q.maxdist(this)))
    45→ *  - maxDist: 
    46→ *    - lazily calculated.
    47→ *    - calculated while excluding subbranches that don't need to be calculated
    48→ *    - Invalidated on modifications (should speed up remove/insert)
    49→ *  - Algorithm 2 (insert) uses BASE=1.3:
    50→ *     BASE*covdist(p)  
    51→ *     instead of
    52→ *     2*covdist(p)) 
    53→ *  - Rebalancing:
    54→ *    - The paper proposes to sort the children on their distance to 'x' and then
    55→ *      insert into the first one that has enough covdist.
    56→ *      The sorting appears unnecessary because we anyway have to check all children,
    57→ *      and finding the closest one is trivially possible without sorting.
    58→ *  - Some optimizations for kNN which are not discussed in the paper
    59→ *  
    60→ * Other:
    61→ * - We also implemented the kNN algorithm by Hjaltason and Samet,
    62→ *   but it about 2x as long as our own algorithm in all scenarios we tested.
    63→ * TODO
    64→ * - Rebalancing (nearest-ancestor)
    65→ * - Merge Node/Point classes
    66→ *     
    67→ * @author Tilmann Zäschke
    68→ */
    69→public class CoverTree<T> implements PointIndex<T> {
